# Three.js Geometry to OBJ Export

## Overview
Exporting Three.js meshes to Wavefront OBJ format requires extracting vertex positions, normals, and face indices from `BufferGeometry`, applying the mesh's world transform, and writing them in OBJ text format.

## OBJ File Format
```
# Wavefront OBJ
v x y z        # Vertex position
vn nx ny nz    # Vertex normal
f v1//n1 v2//n2 v3//n3  # Face (1-indexed)
```

## Using OBJExporter from three/addons

### Installation
```bash
npm install three
```

### Usage with OBJExporter
```javascript
import { OBJExporter } from 'three/addons/exporters/OBJExporter.js';
// or: import { OBJExporter } from 'three/examples/jsm/exporters/OBJExporter.js';

const exporter = new OBJExporter();
const objString = exporter.parse(mesh); // Pass a single mesh or a scene
fs.writeFileSync('output.obj', objString);
```

### Important Notes
- `OBJExporter.parse()` accepts any `Object3D`. If you pass a group, it exports all meshes within it.
- The exporter applies the object's world matrix to vertices automatically.
- Each mesh becomes a named group in the OBJ using `o meshName`.

## Manual OBJ Export (No Dependencies Beyond Three.js)
When you need fine control over what gets exported:

```javascript
function meshToOBJ(mesh) {
    // Ensure world matrix is up to date
    mesh.updateWorldMatrix(true, false);

    const geometry = mesh.geometry;
    const positions = geometry.getAttribute('position');
    const normals = geometry.getAttribute('normal');
    const index = geometry.getIndex();

    let obj = `o ${mesh.name}\n`;

    // Transform vertices to world space
    const vertex = new THREE.Vector3();
    for (let i = 0; i < positions.count; i++) {
        vertex.fromBufferAttribute(positions, i);
        vertex.applyMatrix4(mesh.matrixWorld);
        obj += `v ${vertex.x} ${vertex.y} ${vertex.z}\n`;
    }

    // Transform normals to world space (using normal matrix)
    const normalMatrix = new THREE.Matrix3().getNormalMatrix(mesh.matrixWorld);
    const normal = new THREE.Vector3();
    if (normals) {
        for (let i = 0; i < normals.count; i++) {
            normal.fromBufferAttribute(normals, i);
            normal.applyMatrix3(normalMatrix).normalize();
            obj += `vn ${normal.x} ${normal.y} ${normal.z}\n`;
        }
    }

    // Faces
    if (index) {
        for (let i = 0; i < index.count; i += 3) {
            const a = index.getX(i) + 1;
            const b = index.getX(i + 1) + 1;
            const c = index.getX(i + 2) + 1;
            obj += `f ${a}//${a} ${b}//${b} ${c}//${c}\n`;
        }
    }

    return obj;
}
```

